This keeps the same loop and calls, but checks string length before the full comparison. Mismatched names are rejected without a byte comparison, and `==` on equal-length strings matches `compare() == 0`. I did not hoist `GetNumSubFields()` out of the loop, since that could change observable behavior if it has side effects.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 FieldBase::GetSubField(const std::string& subFieldName) const
{
    const std::size_t wantedSize = subFieldName.size();
    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < this->GetNumSubFields(); i++) {
        const std::string& name = this->GetSubField(i)->name;
        if (name.size() == wantedSize && name == subFieldName)
            return i;
    }

    return FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD;
}
```